Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:01:03 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 107/230] Repoint the suite at the trimmed catalog so npm test
 runs again
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

npm test aborted on import: seedTeams.test.ts and competitions.test.ts still
imported REST_OF_WORLD_LEAGUES and LEAGUES_ALL, both deleted when the catalog
was trimmed to the top 5, so no group ever executed. teamGroups.test.ts then
failed on the old SQL semantics, expecting league-less and international-fixture
sides to classify as "international".

Updates the three suites to assert the new boundary — top-five-only seed scope,
a catalog that is exactly the five leagues, and a classification with no
international branch — instead of deleting the coverage. Verified the updated
assertions still fire by reintroducing the removed export and a stray
rest-of-world row: both made the groups fail as intended.

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
